  1782→\subsection*{A.5.4 \quad Overall Usability and Adoption Ratings (Q6--Q10)}
  1783→
  1784→Figure~\ref{fig:survey-means} shows the mean scores for Q6--Q10 as horizontal bars, with a vertical reference line at the scale midpoint (3.0) and at 4.0. Q6 (token-cost awareness) achieved the highest mean (4.50), confirming that context budget visibility is Tokalator's most impactful outcome. Q9 (overall UI satisfaction, dashboard clarity) yielded a mean of 4.10, with over 80\% of respondents (41/50) rating the sidebar dashboard 4 or 5 --- the result of pin/unpin stability improvements and model-sync fixes shipped in v3.1.2. Q8 (install ease, mean=4.32) confirms strong usability: over 70\% of participants rated installation straightforward (4 or 5), with the Marketplace one-click install path cited by 14 respondents. Q10 (Tokalator Pro interest) scored 3.42, indicating moderate but genuine enterprise demand. Table~\ref{tab:survey-gender} breaks down Q3 and Q10 means by gender.
