  1874→\subsection*{A.5.6 \quad Representative Verbatim Quotes}
  1875→
  1876→The following quotes are drawn verbatim from survey open-text responses (lightly edited for grammar; participant IDs assigned sequentially by submission order; gender noted from the self-identification field):
  1877→
  1878→\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  1879→  \item[\textbf{P07}~(F)] \textit{``/preview showed me my system prompt was eating 4,800 tokens every single turn. I had no idea. I cut it by 60\% and my daily API cost dropped noticeably.''} (\textit{T1 / Q1})
  1880→  \item[\textbf{P14}~(M)] \textit{``I'm writing Turkish comments in my code. The 4-char heuristic said 1,200 tokens but the API said 1,580. That's a 32\% error, which matters when I'm near the limit.''} (\textit{T2 / Q2})
  1881→  \item[\textbf{P19}~(N-B)] \textit{``I appreciated having the token count visible without opening a browser tab. Even knowing \emph{roughly} how many tokens I'm using changed how I approach large refactoring tasks.''} (\textit{Q6})
  1882→  \item[\textbf{P23}~(M)] \textit{``I switched from GPT~5.3 to Claude Opus~4.6 mid-session and Tokalator still showed the GPT~5.3 window size. It took me a minute to realise why the budget numbers looked wrong.''} (\textit{T3 / Q3})
  1883→  \item[\textbf{P31}~(M)] \textit{``Every time I switched tabs, my pinned files would quietly un-pin themselves. I kept re-pinning the same three files before every session. Once the March~6 fix landed it just worked --- pins survived across tab switches without me touching anything.''} (\textit{T4 / Q4})
  1884→  \item[\textbf{P38}~(M)] \textit{``Installation was painless --- two minutes from Marketplace to first token count. That's exactly what a dev tool should feel like.''} (\textit{Q8})
  1885→  \item[\textbf{P42}~(M)] \textit{``/compaction told me I'd hit the threshold in 4 more turns. That was actually useful. But I couldn't tell if it was my open files or the conversation that was growing fastest.''} (\textit{T5 / Q5})
  1886→  \item[\textbf{P48}~(M)] \textit{``I use SSH into a Linux container, so the VS Code extension isn't available. The \texttt{tokalator budget} CLI was the only way I could check my context. Please keep investing in it.''} (\textit{T1 / Q6})
