   172→Several lines of prior work relate to Tokalator's scope. Mei et al.~\cite{mei2025survey} surveyed over 1,400 context engineering papers and mapped the field across context retrieval, processing, management, RAG, memory systems, tool-integrated reasoning, and multi-agent architectures. Tokalator addresses the developer-tooling layer of this landscape: making context budget consumption visible and cost-optimizable directly inside the IDE. Table~\ref{tab:comparison} positions Tokalator against the closest existing tools across eight capability dimensions, including VS Code v1.110~\cite{vscode2026v110}, which introduced native context window indicators and a \texttt{/compact} slash command for Claude agent sessions in February~2026. While VS Code's built-in features address context awareness for Copilot-specific sessions, they do not provide cross-provider cost modeling, per-file relevance scoring, caching break-even analysis, or offline token counting; Tokalator targets this complementary space.
