   198→\textit{Tokenization libraries:} OpenAI's \texttt{tiktoken} and Anthropic's \texttt{claude-tokenizer} provide programmatic token counting for their respective BPE vocabularies~\cite{sennrich2016bpe,openai2025cookbook}. Each provider uses a distinct encoding: OpenAI models use \texttt{cl100k\_base} or \texttt{o200k\_base}, while Anthropic models use their proprietary BPE vocabulary. Anthropic exposes a server-side token counting endpoint via the Messages API~\cite{anthropic2025tokencounting}; Tokalator replicates this client-side via \texttt{@anthropic-ai/tokenizer}, enabling offline, zero-API-call token counts. Neither library offers real-time IDE integration, multi-provider comparison, or cost estimation.
