\section{Test Suite Summary}
\label{app:tests}

Tokalator maintains a comprehensive automated test suite with \textit{124 test cases} across \textit{6 test files}, executed using Jest~30 with ts-jest~29. The test suite runs on every commit through the CI pipeline along with build and lint checks. Table~\ref{tab:tests} summarizes the coverage. Key testing strategies include: (1) mathematical validation of closed-form equations (caching break-even, conversation cost projections, Cobb--Douglas quality) against hand-computed expected values; (2) cross-provider consistency checks to ensure all 14 model profiles have valid pricing, context windows, and tokenizer assignments; (3) edge-case coverage for division by zero, zero-token documents, and empty workspaces; and (4) CSP compliance tests verifying that the dashboard uses event delegation (\texttt{data-action} attributes) instead of inline handlers, and that \texttt{fmtTokens} correctly formats both thousands (K) and millions (M).


\begin{table*}[htp!]
\centering
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{} l l p{0.8cm} p{3.5cm} @{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Component} & \textbf{Test File} & \textbf{Tests} & \textbf{Coverage} \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{4}{@{}l@{}}{\textit{VS~Code Extension (2 files, 37 tests)}} \\
\addlinespace
Model Profiles & \texttt{modelProfiles} & 23 & 14 profiles, uniqueness, fuzzy matching \\
Dashboard Provider & \texttt{contextDashboardProvider} & 14 & CSP nonce, data-action, formatting, message handling \\
\addlinespace
\multicolumn{4}{@{}l@{}}{\textit{Web Platform Library (4 files, 87 tests)}} \\
\addlinespace
Pricing Engine & \texttt{lib/pricing} & 40 & Tiered pricing, Cobb--Douglas, projections \\
Conversation Sim. & \texttt{lib/conversation} & 18 & 3 strategies, $O(T^2)$ validation, turns-for-budget \\
Context Analysis & \texttt{lib/context} & 16 & Token estimation, budget, remaining turns \\
Caching Analysis & \texttt{lib/caching} & 13 & Break-even, ROI, budget optimization \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{2}{@{}l@{}}{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{124} & \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Tokalator test suite summary (v3.1.2). All 124 tests pass across 6 files covering the VS~Code extension (37 tests) and the web platform library (87 tests).}
\label{tab:tests}
\end{table*}


\section{Command Reference}
\label{app:commands}

Table~\ref{tab:commands} lists all commands available in the Tokalator VS~Code extension (v3.1.2).

\begin{table*}[htp!]
\centering
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{} l p{7.5cm} @{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Command} & \textbf{Description} \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{2}{@{}l@{}}{\textit{VS~Code Commands (Command Palette)}} \\
\addlinespace
\texttt{tokalator.refresh} & Refresh token count and rebuild snapshot \\
\texttt{tokalator.optimize} & Run context optimization report \\
\texttt{tokalator.clearPins} & Clear all pinned files \\
\addlinespace
\multicolumn{2}{@{}l@{}}{\textit{Chat Participant Commands (@tokalator)}} \\
\addlinespace
\texttt{/count} & Show current token count and budget status \\
\texttt{/breakdown} & Show per-file token breakdown \\
\texttt{/optimize} & Close low-relevance tabs to free up context \\
\texttt{/pin} & Pin a file (always included, $R = 1.0$) \\
\texttt{/unpin} & Unpin a file (return to normal scoring) \\
\texttt{/model} & Show or switch the active AI model \\
\texttt{/instructions} & List and tokenize instruction files \\
\texttt{/compaction} & Per-turn growth analysis and compaction recommendations \\
\texttt{/preview} & Preview next-turn token cost before sending \\
\texttt{/reset} & Reset session state (turn counter) \\
\texttt{/exit} & End session and save summary \\
\addlinespace
\multicolumn{2}{@{}l@{}}{\textit{MCP Server Tools (\texttt{tokalator-mcp})}} \\
\addlinespace
\texttt{count\_tokens} & Count tokens in a text string or file path using the real Claude BPE tokenizer \\
\texttt{estimate\_budget} & Full budget breakdown for a set of files plus conversation overhead \\
\texttt{preview\_turn} & Preview estimated token cost of the next chat turn with remaining-turn count \\
\texttt{list\_models} & List all Claude model profiles with context windows and rot thresholds \\
\addlinespace
\multicolumn{2}{@{}l@{}}{\textit{CLI Binary (\texttt{tokalator} command)}} \\
\addlinespace
\texttt{tokalator count} & Count tokens in one or more files, or in raw text via \texttt{--text} \\
\texttt{tokalator budget} & Full budget breakdown: files + system overhead + conversation \\
\texttt{tokalator preview} & Preview estimated token cost of the next turn given current token count \\
\texttt{tokalator models} & List available Claude model profiles \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Complete command reference for Tokalator (v3.1.2). The VS~Code extension exposes three Command Palette commands and 11 chat participant slash commands. The MCP server exposes four tools to Claude Code via stdio transport. The CLI binary provides the same four operations from the terminal.}
\label{tab:commands}
\end{table*}


\subsection{Development timeline}

Development spanned from January~31 to March~9, 2026 (38~calendar days, 13~active coding days).
Figure~\ref{fig:commits} shows the daily commit count and net code additions across the thirteen active development days. The highest activity occurred on February~8 (46~commits), which included the core extension build from v0.1.0 through v3.1.1. February~19 (5~commits) added VS~Code~1.109 agent-skills and hooks documentation, wiki fetch scheduling, and events-page fixes. March~6 (1~commit) added the paper, MCP server, and updated wiki articles and events. March~7 (11~commits) delivered the v3.1.2 release with model auto-sync, pin/unpin fix, real screenshots, and documentation updates. March~9 (1~commit) added the evaluation framework, pure scorer extraction, session logger, and experiment scripts (+1.4K~LOC).



